    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369-a1">

                <pb facs="0542" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg532"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>There is set forth below a list of the draft directives prepared by the U.S.
                    Advisers, EAC, and not acted upon separately by SWNCC or JCS. In the right hand
                    column are set forth the paragraphs of JCS 1067/6, as revised by JCS 1067/8,
                    which deal particularly with the subject matter of the draft directives:</p>
                <table cols="2" rows="11">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. Disposition of Political Prisoners, JCS
                            Memo 326</cell>
                        <cell>13</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>. War Criminals, JCS Memo 332, briefly
                            touched upon (a separate directive is in the course of
                                preparation)<anchor n="85" xml:id="d369-f1"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>8</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>. Dissolution of the Nazi Party and Purge
                            of Nazi Personnel, JCS Memo 334</cell>
                        <cell>6</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>. Property Control, JCS Memo 322</cell>
                        <cell>6, 15, 29 and 48</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>. Control of Food and Agriculture, JCS
                            Memo 329</cell>
                        <cell>27 and 28</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">f</hi>. Control of Labor, JCS Memo 333</cell>
                        <cell>23 to 26 inclusive</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">g</hi>. Control of Coal Industry, JCS Memo
                            339</cell>
                        <cell>34<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">h</hi>. Control of Oil Industry, JCS Memo
                            347</cell>
                        <cell>30, 32 and 34</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">i</hi>. Control of Internal Trade, JCS Memo
                            348</cell>
                        <cell>16, 18, 21 and 22</cell>
                    </row>
                    <pb facs="0543" n="533" xml:id="pg533"/>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">j</hi>. Control of Foreign Trade, JCS Memo
                            349</cell>
                        <cell>40, 41, 42, 49 and 50</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">k</hi>. Control of Educational Institutions in
                            Germany, JCS Memo 309</cell>
                        <cell>14</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </div>
